# --- build outputs and caches: on disk, not in git (the files to print are in print/) -------------------------------
enclosures/*/out/
enclosures/*/hardware/cache/
# ... and what prepare_hardware.py and hw.py regenerate from the board: kicad-cli's input copy and log, the board
# mesh (python src/hw.py; only the 4.26 review.py reads it) and the board summary (the 4.26's hw.py writes it here;
# no code reads it, and the 3.68's hw.py writes its own to out/<variant>/)
enclosures/*/hardware/silkscreen_pcb-portable.kicad_pcb
enclosures/*/hardware/step-export.log
enclosures/*/hardware/board.stl
enclosures/*/hardware/mechanical.json
# OrcaSlicer rewrites its log in the folder it runs from on every slice
00000.log
# the showcase adapters' outputs (showcase/gen/adapt_*.py --out default)
showcase/build/
# the case showcase's generated data (about 38 MB; rebuild with python -B showcase/gen/bundle.py --strict-page),
# and the two assets the bundle copies in (sources: showcase/page/strip.json, docs/images/optics_heatmaps.png)
docs/showcase/strip.json
docs/showcase/optics_heatmaps.png
docs/showcase/core-*.json
docs/showcase/build-*.json
docs/showcase/extras-*.json
docs/showcase/data-*.json
docs/showcase/models-*.js
